        "date": "2026-11-10T05:59:01Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(machines): a plasma machine kind and the Tormach 1300PL\n\nA `.mch` may declare `\"kind\": \"plasma\"`: X/Y cut, Z is the torch lifter,\nno spindle. The plasma rules (no spindle keys, live tool, coolant or\nrotary) refuse by name at the reader and the Machines pane's validator\nfrom one list (post::machine::plasma_refusals), and Machine::is_sane\nholds them for project files. The machine check on a plasma table judges\nX/Y travel and feed and the changer count, refuses non-plasma ops and\nspindle rpm by name, and skips Z depth/travel and rpm with named\nMachineCheck notes (shown on the status line's machine vote). The\ncommand door refuses milling/turning ops on a plasma setup; no post\nserves a plasma table until the plasma post ships (PLASMA_POSTS).\n\nThe Tormach 1300PL ships (UM10720 v1223A §2.2.1, p.16; spec sheet\n03/24): X 48.5 / Y 50 / Z 3.9 in (the smaller of manual and sheet),\n1000 IPM X/Y, 120 IPM Z, rapid unstated, inch, one torch (Tool 1).\nKerf is the torch tool's diameter (docs/decisions/669-plasma-kind.md).\n\nKind moves to post/src/machine/kind.rs and the check's per-move helpers\nto app/src/machine/judge.rs (400-line law).\n\nFixes #669\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
