      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T06:46:13Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(plasma): a plasma profile operation - kerf, leads, cut direction, small holes, inner first\n\nA torch tool kind (ToolKind::Torch): its diameter is the kerf width (the\neditor labels it \"Kerf width\"), no corner, rpm 0 by law - a torch stating\nan rpm is refused by name at AddTool / ChangeTool / the library reader;\nPT-KERF-150 (1.5 mm) ships in the catalog; the kind round-trips the\nproject file.\n\nThe Plasma Profile (OpType 39, appended; Family::Plasma, Section::Plasma)\ncuts picked closed contours and open runs - or the model's through-\nsilhouette - through the plate in one pass at the plate top (+ the cut\nheight when stated). Kerf offset by kerf/2 to the waste side in the\ncomputer by default; G41/G42 as the option (CompSpans carry the part\ncontour with straight engage / cancel leads at least the kerf radius\nlong). Outer contours CW, holes CCW (Hypertherm); `reversed` flips both\nand says so. Arc lead-in / lead-out on the waste side (halved when they\nfind no room, noted; refused past that). Small holes (Ø < 32 mm or\n< 1.5x thickness, LinuxCNC Plasma Primer §13): pierce at the centre,\nperpendicular lead-in, no lead-out, optional overburn, 65 % feed.\nCut order is the nesting tree's post-order - an island before its hole,\nevery hole before its part's outline. Feed, pierce height, cut height and\npierce delay are optional (blank = the controller's AutoFS). The\ngenerator certifies a kerf law: no lit move's kerf reaches the part.\nDegenerate input - zero-length or collinear contours, self-crossing\ncontours or runs, kerf <= 0, a hole the kerf cannot enter (named by\ncontour id), a pinched gap - is refused by name.\n\nThe CL carries the plasma record for #671 / #672 (Toolpath::plasma,\ncl::PlasmaCut / TorchSpan): `; PLASMA KERF<um> [CONTROL] [PIERCE<um>]\n[CUTH<um>] [DELAY<ms>] [AUTOFEED] [REVERSED]`, `; TORCH ON C<id>\nOUTER|INNER|OPEN [PARENT<id>] [SMALL<f x1000>]` before the first lit\nmove, `; TORCH OFF C<id>` after the last (.cl v5; text dump and project\npath cache round-trip; docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md). Golden:\ntests/golden/plasma_plate_with_holes.cl.\n\nWired through #669's seams: cuts_plasma answers the family, the family\ndoor names both directions (a mill-turn no longer admits every family),\nthe ribbon shows the Plasma section on a plasma table only, the op page\n(plasma_page.rs), the machine check judges the op's XY travel and feed.\nDecisions: docs/decisions/670-plasma-profile.md.\n\nFixes #670\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
